    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="43aeaeed-d9d8-5875-9be6-b7c2ba4310b2" activityNameId="dc34f524-0a7f-5e80-8804-0726063406c4" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">EKG I, electrical system, office building, construction</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: EKG I, electrical system, office building, construction
Elektroanlagen, tiefer Installationsgrad;
UUID: ac4fb5f0-36d8-3a44-b51b-9ad8355c9796
This data set includes the material use for the manufacturing of the electronic installations in an office building according to Klingler and Kasser, 2011. The source states that 95 % of the mass volume is accounted for, which covers about 100 individual components. 1 office building was taken into account. The energy reference area is 2062 m2 for the basic construction and 1405 m2 for the tenant equipment (Mieterausbau). Basic and tenant"s equipment were taken into account both relative to each energy reference areas. The neon tubes and lamp fitting, as well as the control gear (EVG and VVG) were modelled with an energy saving light bulb. The electrical system has a life-span of 30 years. Transport is included.
Location: Data for Zurich, Switzerland
Technology: Average technology
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: unknown 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_ac4fb5f0-36d8-3a44-b51b-9ad8355c9796.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
